            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "Liquids A and B form an ideal solution in the entire composition range. At $350 \\mathrm{~K}$, the vapor pressures of pure A and pure B are $7 \\times 10^{3} \\mathrm{~Pa}$ and $12 \\times 10^{3} \\mathrm{~Pa}$, respectively. The composition of the vapour is in equilibrium with a solution containing 40 mole percent of $\\mathrm{A}$ at this temperature is:",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "JamXa",
              "text": "$x_{\\mathrm{A}}=0.37 ; x_{\\mathrm{B}}=0.63$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "Rzw9z",
              "text": "$x_{\\mathrm{A}}=0.28 ; x_{\\mathrm{B}}=0.72$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "68eOs",
              "text": "$x_{\\mathrm{A}}=0.4 ; x_{\\mathrm{B}}=0.6$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "93xxO",
              "text": "$x_{\\mathrm{A}}=0.76 ; x_{\\mathrm{B}}=0.24$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "$\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{A}}^{\\circ}=7 \\times 10^{3}$\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{B}}^{\\circ}=12 \\times 10^{3}$\r\n\r\n$x_{\\mathrm{A}}^{\\prime}=0.4 ; x_{\\mathrm{B}}^{\\prime}=1-0.4$\r\n\r\n$x_{\\mathrm{B}}^{\\prime}=0.6$\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{P}_{\\text {total }}=\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{A}^{\\circ}}^{x_{\\mathrm{A}}^{\\prime}}+\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{B}}^{\\circ} x_{\\mathrm{B}}^{\\prime}$\r\n\r\n$=7 \\times 10^{3} \\times 0.4+12 \\times 10^{3} \\times 0.6$\r\n\r\n$=(7 \\times 0.4+12 \\times 0.6) \\times 10^{3}=10^{4}$\r\n\r\n$x_{\\mathrm{A}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{A}^{\\circ}}^{x^{\\prime}} \\mathrm{A}}{\\mathrm{P}_{\\text {total }}}=\\frac{7 \\times 10^{3} \\times 0.4}{10^{4}}$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore x_{\\mathrm{A}}=0.28, x_{\\mathrm{B}}=1-0.28=0.72$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
